<!-- The first step on every leg: every done flag false. Flow variables last the whole exchange (L6), so without it a
     reply leg whose JS-Airs3Init did not finish would run on the request leg's flags and pass the reply unscanned. That
     includes every flag a refusal step's condition reads (phase 3: mode, skipLeg, quiet) and what JS-Airs3Respond and the log
     line read (the route, the outcome, the detections, the scan id), so a run whose JS-Airs3Init is cut is refused as a
     scanner failure and logged as such, whatever the run before it on this exchange was. Not reset: what one run leaves the
     next on purpose (airs3.destreamed, promptContext, promptVerdict, the never-twice marks, and plainReply, the reply as
     JSON that a restream keeps for a later run on the leg).
     An AssignMessage: no time limit can cut it, and if it fails Apigee refuses the call itself. -->
<AssignMessage continueOnError="false" enabled="true" name="AM-Airs3Reset">
  <DisplayName>AM-Airs3Reset</DisplayName>
  <!-- v3.1: both credentials come from the config map alone. A proxy's own variable of either name is emptied here, and
       KVM-GetAIRSConfig then reads the map (an absent entry leaves the variable empty, L26). -->
